---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '@esa/docs/base';
import Section from '@esa/docs/Section.astro';

// `step` is the tier-1 axis rung each role clusters — --shadow-offset-y-050,
// --shadow-blur-050 and so on. The role numbering (1–6) and the ramp numbering
// (050–500) are deliberately independent: one is a set of jobs, the other a scale.
const elevation = [
  { token: '--elevation-1', step: '050', role: 'Resting lift — always-visible surfaces' },
  { token: '--elevation-2', step: '100', role: 'Cards, list items' },
  { token: '--elevation-3', step: '200', role: 'Raised cards; resting rung for unanchored floating controls' },
  { token: '--elevation-4', step: '300', role: 'Dropdowns, popovers, menus, tooltips, toasts' },
  { token: '--elevation-5', step: '400', role: 'Modals, dialogs' },
  { token: '--elevation-6', step: '500', role: 'Full-screen overlays — command palette, entity search' },
];

// The tier-1 material. offset-x is one shared token (every shadow casts straight
// down), so it is not a column here.
const axes = [
  { step: '050', y: '1px',  blur: '4px',  spread: '0',    color: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.03)' },
  { step: '100', y: '2px',  blur: '12px', spread: '0',    color: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04)' },
  { step: '200', y: '4px',  blur: '20px', spread: '-4px', color: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06)' },
  { step: '300', y: '6px',  blur: '24px', spread: '-6px', color: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.07)' },
  { step: '400', y: '8px',  blur: '32px', spread: '-8px', color: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08)' },
  { step: '500', y: '20px', blur: '60px', spread: '0',    color: 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2)'  },
];


const zIndex = [
  { token: '--z-dropdown', value: '50', role: 'Menus, comboboxes' },
  { token: '--z-sidebar', value: '100', role: 'App sidebar' },
  { token: '--z-header', value: '200', role: 'Sticky header / topbar' },
  { token: '--z-modal-backdrop', value: '300', role: 'Dialog scrim' },
  { token: '--z-modal', value: '400', role: 'Dialog surface' },
  { token: '--z-toast', value: '500', role: 'Toasts / notifications' },
  { token: '--z-tooltip', value: '600', role: 'Tooltips (always on top)' },
];
---
<DocsLayout title="Elevation — Ecology" activeHref="/foundations/elevation">
  <nav class="crumbs"><a href={withBase('/')}>Ecology</a> <span>/</span> <span>Foundations</span> <span>/</span> <span>Elevation</span></nav>
  <h1>Elevation</h1>
  <p class="lede">Two systems work together to build depth: soft <strong>shadows</strong> imply lift off the surface, and a fixed <strong>z-index</strong> ladder keeps overlapping layers in a predictable stacking order.</p>

  <Section id="shadows" title="Shadows">
    <p>Deliberately soft and low-contrast — elevation should be felt, not seen. <code>--elevation-*</code> is the full public surface: these six tokens <em>are</em> the shadows, assembled from the tier-1 axes below. Components read these and nothing else.</p>
    <p><strong>Hover is not a rung.</strong> Every rung names a <em>kind of surface</em>; a hover lift moves an element one rung up from wherever it rests. Rung 3 used to be described as “raised cards, hover state,” and being the only rung that named an interaction is why it became the drawer everything lifted got thrown into — six dropdown surfaces sat on it instead of rung 4.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      {elevation.map((s) => (
        <div class="card" style={`box-shadow: var(${s.token})`}>
          <code>{s.token}</code>
          <span class="card__primitive">step {s.step}</span>
          <span class="card__role">{s.role}</span>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section id="shadow-axes" title="Shadow axes">
    <p>The tier-1 material each role clusters. A box-shadow has four axes plus a colour, and splitting them is what makes a shadow themeable — re-point <code>--shadow-color-*</code> and every elevation retints. <code>--shadow-offset-x</code> is a single shared token, not a ramp, because every shadow in the kit casts straight down.</p>
    <table class="z-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Step</th><th>offset-y</th><th>blur</th><th>spread</th><th>color</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {axes.map((a) => (
          <tr>
            <td><code>{a.step}</code></td>
            <td class="z-table__val">{a.y}</td>
            <td class="z-table__val">{a.blur}</td>
            <td class="z-table__val">{a.spread}</td>
            <td class="z-table__role">{a.color}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </Section>

  <Section id="z-index" title="Z-index">
    <p>Overlay layers reference these tokens instead of ad-hoc numbers, so stacking conflicts can't happen. The order is canonical — tooltips always win.</p>
    <table class="z-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Token</th><th>Value</th><th>Layer</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {zIndex.map((z) => (
          <tr>
            <td><code>{z.token}</code></td>
            <td class="z-table__val">{z.value}</td>
            <td class="z-table__role">{z.role}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </Section>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: var(--spacing-500, 1.5rem); padding: var(--spacing-300, 0.75rem) var(--spacing-100, 0.25rem) var(--spacing-500, 1.5rem); }
  .card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px; background: var(--color-background-elevation-raised, #fff); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default-subtle, #efefef); border-radius: var(--radius-400, 0.75rem); padding: var(--spacing-400, 1rem); min-height: 96px; }
  .card code { font-family: var(--typography-font-family-mono, monospace); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-content-default, #171717); }
  .card__primitive { font-family: var(--typography-font-family-mono, monospace); font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #646464); }
.card__role { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #646464); }

  .z-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; border: 1px solid var(--color-border-default, #e5e5e5); border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; }
  .z-table th { text-align: left; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #525252); padding: var(--spacing-250, 0.625rem) var(--spacing-400, 1rem); background: var(--color-background-elevation-sunken, #f5f5f5); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-default, #e5e5e5); }
  .z-table td { padding: var(--spacing-250, 0.625rem) var(--spacing-400, 1rem); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-default-subtle, #efefef); font-size: 14px; }
  .z-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .z-table td code { font-family: var(--typography-font-family-mono, monospace); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--color-content-default, #171717); }
  .z-table__val { font-family: var(--typography-font-family-mono, monospace); color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #525252); }
  .z-table__role { color: var(--color-content-default-secondary, #646464); }
</style>
